025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":18,"created_at":"2025-05-08T20:17:36Z","updated_at":"2025-07-09T16:38:33Z","closed_at":"2025-07-09T16:38:31Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.5.dev3\n- Not reproducible in: 4.4.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev3 - Arch Linux #1 ZEN SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Tue, 29 Apr 2025 09:23:22 +0000 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (RPL-P) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900H (20 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nGodot's occlusion culling seems to only cull objects when looking at them from certain angles. The commit that resulted in this change is 18eb1c1072eba9032efb35a3b6e1039511700548\n\nThis is a video to demonstrate it in 4.5.dev3. The camera is inside of an OccluderInstance3D with a box shape.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ba5645f4-8c53-47b5-9faf-be2d25f184ad\n\nIn 4.4.1, it happens to a much lesser extent:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4fe857df-30cc-4d24-92f4-98b5b42ccb17\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add some MeshInstance3Ds to a scene\n2. Create a new OccluderInstance3D with a BoxOccluder3D as the shape\n3. Put the camera inside the OccluderInstance3D and look around\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[occlusion_culling_test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20109939/occlusion_culling_test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/